1,'Straight out of the box this product has a musty, sour-like, spoiled smell. As if the product has gone bad. It smells disgusting. Truly pure essential oils do not go rancid; I do understand that they can lose their potenty over time. This bottle has lovely packaging but the company does not give dates of manufacture. Nor do they speficy where the lavender is sourced from; which was a bit of a red flag before I made the purchase. Nearly all of the REAL lavender oils I have purchased and used in the past state what country the lavender came from/is sourced from. I should have just bypassed it. My sole reason for stepping outside of the three brands I regularly use is those brands were out of stock.<br /><br />So far the only pro to this product is that the packaging is quite pretty...that is not what I needed to be delivered to me. I needed lavender oil.<br /><br /> Per the box: “non-toxic; biodegradable; made in the USA; sustainably sourced; free from parabens, sulfates, preservatives, and synthetics; vegan + cruelty free” and “100\% pure”....I have my doubts.<br /><br />Truly good, worthwhile products have consistency; they are not hit or miss batch wise. Whatever I got is not a good or worthwhile, and due to my work hours I do not have time to be tying to make it to drop locations to return this stuff. Keep searching folks...buy a different brand; don’t waste your money.',B0765B4HMV,AHDXASEPNJF4QQF4DRWCXWULNQJQ
