3,'The oil is okay. It does what it is supposed to do. It\'s the packaging that is the problem.<br /><br />Although it is labeled \"baby oil\" many women use it in the shower or bath to moisturize our skin. Once steam or water hits the bottle, the labels on front and back will peel off almost immediately. Also: the bottle gets very slippery, and there is no way to hold onto it if your hands have the oil on them. The bottle has no texture or shape that enables one to hold it if a little oil spills down the sides. This is why I put rubber bands around it. One more example of poor package design is the cap, which is a struggle to remove.<br /><br />Addendum: The cap came apart.<br /><br />Buy the oil, but put it in another bottle.',B07XJ1N2JN,AFIAKCDUPFMCKVYAPB7EHPUDVM5Q
