1,'Supposed to be compatible with Norelco Bodygroom 2034 but did not work. Couple of issues made this a \"don\'t buy\".  First of all the battery tabs are extremely thin and backwards polarity then the original so you can\'t solder in directly. I ended up flipping the battery over and attaching thin wires between the tab and board to make it work. Checked it all and put it together to charge. The charging light flashed normally so left it on overnight. In the morning it was dead. No juice, no orange or green light. So opened it all back up and checked - only showed 1.1 volts across the terminals. Essentially one of the cells died overnight rendering the package useless for me. So 5 hours wasted and $9.99 down the drain :(',B06Y2KD2Y6,AHC4JYQQ5PORDB7QQM6OTZSVYF5Q
