4,'Jan 2023 Update: Looking through my old reviews and updating. This brush miraculously still functions. It’s still good for smoothing out a bit of frizz, but not actual straightening. I figured out a hack to clean it: Use a disinfectant wipe, and the end of a rat tail hairbrush to drag the wipe between the bristles. Over the years the brush has this burning chemical smell whenever it is used and this smell can get into your hair. The brush has served me well, but I will upgrade from it this year!<br /><br />2018: Very nice. This takes half the time as a normal straightener. It will be perfect if you are fixing slight waves in your hair.<br />I had very curly hair before I permed it straight and made this work. However as my roots are growing out now, I notice that it’s kind of hard to reach roots with this. It’s also difficult to clean; take a wet cotton swab and get any dried product as best you can.',B016YKQ4PY,AF5TDMGTANFIKNZYQQPB6BQJ4MMQ
