4,'I use these as normal replacement insoles, not to address any particular foot issues.  I found that they do conform somewhat to your foot as advertised -- it can take a couple of weeks.  Overall, I like them and consider them a nice upgrade from my OEM insoles (that were getting a bit worn).<br /><br />A few things to note:<br />* You need to allow a couple of weeks for these to conform to your foot<br />* I found these to be thinner than other insoles I have tried, especially in the toe area where they are quite thin.  They are similar in thickness to factory OEM insoles that come in your shoes.<br />* They don\'t have the very aggressive arch support that you get with many insoles on the market, so if you are looking for extra arch support or any other \"corrective\" features, these may not be the best choice<br />* They seem a bit pricey (currently shown for ~$70) for replacement insoles.  They do have the nice feature of adapting somewhat to your feet, but I am not sure I would pay that much extra for this feature.<br /><br />SUMMARY:<br />A nice set of replacement insoles that adapt to your feet, but a bit on the pricey side -- perhaps the price will come down a bit.',B08HGB21VK,AHNIWV6SX76RSYNUAUSFLYFEWQRA
