5,'The Pandemic has changed our lives in so many ways. Had never heard of hypochlorite before reading about disinfectants. This tiny tool turns tap water and salt into the disinfectant hypochlorite in a matter of minutes that you can then dilute according to the enclosed instructions to clean your home. Amazing! Within a 1/2 hour I had made 3 batches of it and filled 3 spray bottles (at proper dilution). It has a clean fresh essence - not really an odor - but a slight smell when the \"brewing\" of 5 minutes has been completed. When you spray it on a surface they suggest leaving it 1 minute before wiping dry. There is no residual smell, only  a clean essence. You\'ll know it when you use it that it is cleaning. I read alot of research on how this works to kill germs and viruses. It\'s tiny but it does a big job! Make your own hypochlorite - I paid less for this gadget than I paid for a pint of pre-made hypochlorite on Amazon, and I made 3 quart spray bottles of it in less than 30 minutes with just tap water and a few spoonfuls of household salt (I used pink Himalayan salt).  You will need the plug end for the usb cord that goes into the wall socket. If you have a cellphone, you can use that plug and insert the enclosed usb cord. Very happy with this purchase!',B08921H8BF,AG6SQXVRP6QFF623YUVYRCLFEA5A
