3,'I have used one bottle of this &#34;Traditional&#34; product and I still have reservations about it\'s quality. My opinion of MediSILVER is based on the four bottles of MediSILVER BLACK I have used. I fell that the &#34;Black&#34; has a little more strength or effectiveness than the Amber&#34; type. One bottle of the &#34;Black&#34; started to turn to a lighter color part way through and one bottle turned almost clear, by the time there was 1/3 left. My research on Colloidal Silver tells me that color change is improperly suspended silver and when it does that, the product becomes less effective or not effective at all. The key is the small silver particles being suspended in the liquid, for proper absorption in your body, when taken.<br /><br />The same thing will happen to Colloidal Silver if it freezes. It will turn clear and will appear a little cloudy at the bottom. When that happens.... the bottle is Ruined! This MediSIVER may be less costly, but it has never happened to the 10 or so bottles of MesoSilver 20 ppm Colloidal Silver, 500 mL, which I have taken. I have chronic Candida and Colloidal Silver seems to be the best treatment for it. I have become resistant to many of the other products and treatments for Candida.<br /><br />There are other good quality Colloidal Silver products out there, just be careful and do not buy it if the bottle is tinted as it is most likely and impostor (Silver Ions). Also, do not attempt to make it at home with an Ion Generator. That is also Silver Ions, and is not nearly as effective.',B00ADQ5VWS,AHFXOQ42Y5ZR4TP3TB5NKWYKD5DQ
