5,'For years I have struggled to try to clean my service dog\'s teeth with a small round soft bristle toothbrush.  Always difficult and exhausting to try to get him to let me into his small toy poodle mouth-especially the back. Often the brush made his gums bleed.  Poor fellow has lost many teeth over the last couple years to bacterial problems common in his breed.  My hesitancy to brush him due to the stress it induced in both of us didn\'t help.  I have 45 of my own health issues due to Agent Orange exposure.  For me the need for easy care and a life as stress free as possible is paramount.<br /><br />I just discovered these PenVinoo cloth finger brushes and am so happy I gave them a try.  Just a thumb and index finger and I am covering both sides of the mouth at the same time. Additionally, they are even easier to wrap behind the teeth which I could not do with a brush. So far I have not experienced any gum bleeding which certainly makes momma more likely to want to brush again tomorrow too.<br /><br />These cloud soft cots seem to be way less traumatic for my pup.  He isn\'t showing any signs of discomfort or fighting to get me out of his mouth anymore.  I am not planning on rewashing the cots. I know that may be a cost saver but they fit perfect now and I would think they would shrink a bit in a wash and dry situation.  Plus I\'d rather not have dog toothpaste in my washing machine.<br /><br />I\'ve just ordered another 200 finger brushes as my Vet wants me to brush daily whenever possible.<br /><br />Whether these would fit a larger man comfortably I cannot say.  I am a female with hands that fit size medium disposable gloves.  They fit just about perfect.  They may stretch to the smaller spectrum of size large.<br /><br />Buy one package and see if you, too, can reduce some stress out of both you and your pups life with the easiest brushing concept I have ever encountered.',B09NBFDSGF,AFV7MM5MS6SG7WT3ZRHA4HWSX4TA
4,'I just received this toner for free for review and I absolutely love it! I\'ve been using it for a couple days now because I wanted to give my skin time to react to it and so far my skin hasn\'t had any negative reactions. The packaging is very nice and feels high end which I appreciate. The spray bottle sprays a super fine mist that doesn\'t shock you when it squirts out and makes it easy to evenly spritz your face. I really like that because a lot of facial sprays have terrible misters and I have to put the product into a not her bottle but not with this one! The scent is a bit strong but it\'s nice. Not like anything I\'ve ever smelled before. Very earthy and natural. I think the strongest smells are the geranium and the witch hazel so if you like those scents you\'ll love  this! As for the actual product, I like it a lot so far!  It\'s gentle and calming and doesn\'t completely strip my face leaving it tight and dry but it still removes just as much dirt and oil as the toners I regularly use. This is my first spray on toner and I really live how easy and refreshing it is! I\'m really interested in trying more products from Valentia now because I\'ve really enjoyed this one and I highly recommend it!',B01H578LZQ,AHDWMQKZ6TJ7K5PVTG5AIQF363DA
