5,'First impression.... damn, is this comfy!  Really.  It doesn\'t cup the eyes.  So it will put light pressure on the eyes, unless you want to wear it loose.  And it doesn\'t cut out all light, but 90\% is just great.  But it\'s so comfortable to wear, it\'s just a joy to have on.<br /><br />For the longest time, I was using velcro sleep masks that cup the eyes and shut out nearly all the light.  But I\'ve always had the same problem.... they lose their contour over time and the thin strap is irritating around or over the ears and then twists itself over time to where it can\'t be untwisted.  My current one has just lost nearly all its hold because its all twisted up.  And I have to tie it in a knot just so it doesn\'t fall off while I\'m sleeping (the knot is really uncomfortable, if that comes as a surprise).<br /><br />But this one... wow.  Its like a really cuddly bear hugging your face.  It even cushions the ears!  I didn\'t know I\'d like that so much.  The strap is a couple inches thick and just ends up hugging your whole face.  Because it\'s so soft on the inside, its like having a face pillow. But it\'s dense enough that it cuts out almost all light.  So it doesn\'t contour around the face like my other one.  That\'s overrated.  Try this.  Please.  =D',B07PC11C33,AH4PEV3GHRUJ5MG6LQ36S4HMPITQ
