3,'Hair Straightener Brush,Oak Leaf Detangling Hair Brush<br />Did not care for this straightening &#34;brush&#34; very much.<br />1st off, the brush is a little heavy! The so-called &#34;bristles&#34; are very hard & they are spread rather far apart from one another with a high projection, which made it harder to truly get the hair straight, especially since it didn\'t grip my hair. And, since the bristles have a high projection, it was difficult to straighten my hair close to the scalp and the very ends too. It felt as though it just slid over the very top of my hair without my hair really getting into the brush. In order to use it, I had to the really pull sections of my hair taut with one hand and push the brush into and down the section of hair to see any real results.I feel that it &#34;my&#34; work better on thicker hair. (Even the image that I have found below states that it is for THICK curly hair)  I had to try really hard to get my hair to make contact because it\'s thinner.<br />I received this product at a discount in exchange for an honest and unbiased review.',B01CU0Z4JE,AGNXLLIDXBCA773GWDA3CBXYUANA
