5,'I have bought vitamin D3 gels in both 2000 IU and 5000 IU sizes, and usually 5000 IUs is larger, but these are the same size as the 2000 IU gels I have seen.  Not necessarily a problem, but interesting.  I don\'t think vitamin D3 is expensive, so I doubt there is any deception going on.<br /><br />I have read that it is best to take vitamin D dissolved in oil (like this) rather than in powder form because we absorb it better.  And while 2000 IUs is plenty for most adults, seniors don\'t absorb nutrients as well, so I\'ve seen it recommended that we get 5000 IUs/day.  So I think these gels are just what seniors should be taking.',B09VS99BR6,AF2GAWA6A4LYR6LFUCHZJJE4EUFQ
1,'As an experienced vaping industrialist/enthusiast, I\'m always vigilant for economical, yet superior  methods and resources to produce an optimal experience.<br />I gave Essential Depot\'s Vegetable Glycerin an opportunity to prove its practical applications to that in our community. Although it be economic, it is very misleading with its &#34;USP-Kosher-Food Grade&#34; claim and left me questioning their latest manufacturing standards, any quality control protocols and marketing strategies in practice.<br /><br />My experience using this liquid was very uncomfortable; resulting with nausea, a numbed-mouth sensation, and &#34;foggy&#34; mentality after a few &#34;draws&#34; from quality testing my initial trial batch.<br />The only deviation from my formula and chemical synthesis was substituting this vegetable glycerin to which I would normally utilize.<br />This naturally lead me to believe the allowed tolerance of arsenic, chlorides, sulphates, etc. have increased or some form of contamination occurred during the manufacturing process.<br /><br />Although this may be favorable for other applications other than vaping, I COULD NOT RECOMMEND this vegetable glycerin for DIY electronic liquid manufacturing. I ask that  Essential Depot update the Certificate of Analysis / Spec Sheet for this product (last certified 2012) and suggest you proceed with EXTREME CAUTION should you disregard this warning.',B004C7MTLA,AHJB3EOVWNHXRVTJ3FT7DJIIBOMA
