1,'I have 3 children ages 4-8, all with sensory issues, all orally fixated.  I bought both the rectangle and the round pendants.  My hope was that these pendant chews would keep them from chewing their sleeves, fingers, toys, etc, and not got lost or end up dirty/on the floor.  I put them on long necklaces for the kids to wear.  My 4 year old promptly took off the necklace, swung it around in circles and ended up hitting his pre-k classmates with it.  My 6 year old threw it in the trash, and said chewing on his sleeve was more enjoyable because this didn\'t \"feel good.\"  My 8 year old also used it to distract her classmates, swinging it around, etc.  So I bought these retractable pulleys that clipped to their belt loops.  My 4 year old broke the retractable pulley after 5 minutes and was banned from bringing his chewy to pre-school, and has not used it since.  My 8 year old took it off the clip and lost it.  Bottom line is, these pendants are very hard, and most kids are looking for something they can chew on for sensory input, but these are too solid/firm.  So for us, what sounded like a great solution did not work at all.  I wish I hadn\'t wasted my money.',B004NRB26C,AGCWOV5VSIGK7USNU34B5JC5MWDQ
5,'This footrest is built like other similar items on the market.  It\'s basically half a cylinder.  You can use it flat side down or curved side down which has some versatility.  I prefer curved side down because I fidget.  The fabric is a nice soft touch velvety velour material.  The footrest is soft but just firm enough.  There are 2 parts, the main footrest and a 2nd rectangle that can be used to add additional height if necessary.  I do not use this as the rest by itself is fine.  I have 2 of these type footrests and my cats enjoy sleeping on the extra pieces that I don\'t use, so, bonus! The flat bottoms of both pieces have textured silicone dots to give traction when placed on the floor and these work well.<br /><br />I like this footrest but I do not like sitting with my feet together at my desk and at about 17\" my feet want to naturally be just beyond the edges of this footrest.  I think 24 or 30\" would be a better length for me which is why I now have 2. If you tend to sit with your feet together or closer than 17\" this will work fine.  If you need more width I think having 2 of these side by side works fine.',B088LHV16Z,AGNKAU3YBJNB3LYEPZ6PA3GFS7PA
