5,'1) Looks great - I get many positive comments on this light<br />2) Sturdy / metal construction - the base is heavy which keeps the lamp stationary even if I bump the lamp/desk.<br />3) Does not get hot.  Warm yes, but not dangerously so (disclaimer: lamps can be dangerous so don\'t touch it / try to sue me if you manage to burn yourself).<br />4) Reduces headaches / eye strain - when I first turned on the lamp I thought the light appeared too &#34;blue&#34; and maybe a bit abrasive compared to a 65-watt incandescent or even a florescent.  However, after 3 months of use I could not be happier.  I am chained to my desk studying for several hours a day.  Before this lamp I experienced eye strain/burning and headaches.  With this lamp I am able to stay focused longer, and avoid headaches and burning/tired eyes.<br /><br />5) It\'s a specialty bulb so I do worry that after the expected 10k hour life I might have trouble finding a replacement.',B000YQRATO,AENEDCXRXBC7KVM3JLYOBU7MGXDA
4,'We bought these to make changing poopy diapers easier, and that is what these do. When she wets, we throw the liner with the diapers into the washer. When our baby poops, we just throw the liner away. We throw the liners away because after seeing how long they hold up in the washer, I can\'t see how they could be good for the toilet. I have washed some of the liners a dozen times or more and they still are completely intact. I don\'t dry them because they dry almost instantly on their own when I take them from the washer. I just stack them nicely and set them aside. Overall, we are pleased. This roll of 100 will last us a very long time. We still have 3/4 of the roll completely untouched after several weeks.',B002LRAPNC,AFC6KZD4SRFUBOHE6PZFLYHQJ6LQ
