5,'(Read last paragraph for proper application.)<br />I’ve tried about every brand and type of adhesive bandage out there to keep my prescription estrogen patch on.  And keep it dry when I shower. Finally success with this product!  I’ve included a photo. I’ve had this adhesive film over my patch for 4 days so far, and have showered and the patch is still in place and dry.  It’s not bulky, and it doesn’t lose its adhesive quality like all the other things I’ve tried.  I haven’t tried to remove it yet since I don’t change patches but every 7 days, but I’ve read others saying it was easy to remove.<br />BE SURE YOU DON’T REMOVE THE “OUTER” EDGE COVERING “UNTIL” THE PATCH IS STUCK IN PLACE. That outer edge keeps acts like a picture frame that keeps a canvas from wrinkling (and in this case, prevents it sticking to itself.)  Once the inner portion is stuck to your skin, there is a cut in the framed outer edge that allows you to peel it off in a long strip.<br /><br />I decided to MOVE my patch to a different spot, and discovered the clear adhesive film is easy and painless to pull off. Then I applied my medical patch with a NEW clear adhesive film to a new spot. All went extremely well. You cannot re-use the clear adhesive film; use a new one when you need to reapply.<br /><br />I love this adhesive film!',B01MZD97VL,AHVJD5ZQEHLIE74LS3HELIMYAAPA
