5,'[[VIDEOID:60113d9fe849cfe6248fa74dfed0bdc1]] Summary: As a person who bites their nails, plays with knives, and regularly cuts their toenails too short these are a game changer. They keep a bandaid on easily, keep water out, and reduce pain from an injured finger.<br /><br />Background: I cut off a chunk of my middle finger two days ago at work, and they gave me a bandaid and a blue \"finger condom\" as they called it. It immediately made my life easier. I had painful cuts on two other fingers from a woodworking project and cut one of my toenails too short (causing slight pain to walk lol), so I figured these would come in handy.<br /><br />Shipping: I ordered them at around 3 am on nov 9 with 2 day shipping, they came nov 10 (1 day early. That was nice!) They came in a white box (pictured) sealed in plastic.<br /><br />Sizing: they are a little over two inches long, so they don\'t make it all the way to the base of my longest finger but do on the others. They snugly fit on all my fingers and toes, but are a bit tight on my thumb and big toe. At work I use medium sized vinyl glove. For further size reference, I am female with average sized hands and abnormally long toes. I cut one of the cots shorter for my thumb (see last photo) and it is no longer too tight.<br /><br />Material/durability: these are made of latex, and seem to be about as thick as a typical latex glove. They seem pretty durable. I tested it by both slicing and poking it with a knife (seen in video). It is obviously not cut proof but it took a fair amount of pressure with a knife to slice through it, and I dragged it across the serrated edge and it did not break. It took a relatively hard poke to make a hole. For the price, they are much more durable than I expected. The latex has a pretty good grip on everything, but that may go down with longer use. They do not roll up my finger at all. Even the one I cut short is staying on my thumb with no problem. With no bandaid they work with a touch screen, but with a band aid on underneath it it is harder to use the touch screen.<br /><br />All in all, pretty amazing for the price. If you are bigger than a size medium in gloves/id you are a grown man I\'d recommend getting these ones in a larger size.',B089223T4Y,AEMLXVH5EUEFWK2SL6RSFSPLWSFQ
1,'I am not happy with these cotton pads at all. The are hard to the touch or at least are hard to my touch. I was expecting something more like a cotton pad and these are more like paper towels. If they came in a large size I would think they were paper towels.<br /><br />I do not much absorbency as well because they are very thin.<br /><br />Not the best. You do get a lot for the money but I do not think the money spent is worth it because of the product itself.',B08TMKBSW7,AEAULPMFJAJ3LY45DFUK6XBYJJUA
5,'Dr. Pen M8 is a beast at unleashing intense treatment that softened both my unsightly stretch marks and my cavernous furrows. It not only helped the healing of additional surgical scarring, it hydrated and brightened my complexion. I’m not sure if I’m more impressed by all of its many benefits or the fact I was able to experience its goodness while sitting on my love sofa!',B09BQYWTNT,AF4UB2PGVLHK45WF7I6OED36OQDA
