5,'I’ve been using a traditional foam roller for quite sometime now and heard about vibrating foam rollers. I got to try Hyper Ice’s version and it was pretty good. The big issue is that it was really steep in price. Just wasn’t worth the purchase with what it did. So I kept searching and heard about this brand from a friend who had one and recommended it to me. I’m usually more cautious when it comes to spending money on products I don’t really know about. But I was fortunate enough to be able to try it first at his house before I decided on taking my chances. And I loved it. It worked great. It had 3 power modes and it was rigged with a pattern surface that dig deeper into your muscles than a traditional foam roller. I took pictures of my traditional foam roller next to the omega-3 version so you could see the size difference and contours. Surprisingly I spent about the same amount for the foam roller pictures with no vibration than I did this one. But I guess that was a little while back before these were popular. But anyway so believe this is a great buy. If you workout and run as much as I do (5-6 days a week, for about an hour) And i’d Say it’s definitely worth the purchase. So I’m giving it 5 stars for quality, durability, design, and price.',B07CWJBKPP,AG7WCMXPFZX4KJGBQJ2DVDROMXXA
