4,'So I got this for the office as they seem to expect us work on site folks to match the hours of work from home people, which means live there.<br />Suffice it to say my backside was sore each day, my legs ached and I wasn\'t happy.<br />Read a few reviews and settled on this over the double version.<br />Its certainly comfortable, though for the first two weeks after getting it my back started hurting. Probably because my posture had to adjust.<br />Now that I have acclimated, I can make a good judgment on it.<br />1: its soft and comfortable. My legs have not hurt from excessive chair contact since getting it.<br />2: plopping down onto the seat is a revelation. I literally bounce on this thing.<br />3: As I am not overweight, I could have probably done just fine with the double version as its ever so slightly less thick, weighs less and cost less.<br />4: this thing is thick and heavy. You could probably use it as a punching bag if you could roll it up and find a way to hang it. For my frame (6ft 190lbs), it might be a tad but overkill.<br />5: it smells bad for a couple of days after opening. Do what I did, toss it outside or in a garage for two days before use or be prepared to be nerve gassed.',B01CKMP21W,AGT5D56664C7GBCLAISR7BT3VZDA
