5,'I started having severe migraines with vertigo, auras and multiple types of visual symptoms about 9 months ago.  My symptoms are greatly exacerbated by fluorescent lights and bright lights indoors.  These glasses have saved me.  I had been using a pair of glasses with tinted lenses that were slightly helpful, but they were not filtering out any light spectrum and they were not blocking out light from above or from the side.  These glasses do both.  I have found the especially helpful in stores, doctor\'s offices and waiting rooms, and classrooms.  I am trying to return to the work force and I don\'t think I would have even considered trying before I got these glasses.  I will be purchasing another pair in the next few days that I can wear over my prescription reading glasses.  These have reduced the frequency and intensity of headaches and other migraine symptoms that were caused by light sensitivity.<br /><br />The only issues I found with them is that they were slipping down my nose.  This is due to the bridge of my nose being narrow and not because of a fault of the glasses.  This was remedied by purchasing stick on silicone nose pads.',B00G2KKECG,AFB35LZZSYO6M4P6ZKDWSGYHQUSQ
