5,'I have seasonal, pretty much year round allergies.  Dirt, grass, cat, dog, molds, trees... you name it!  Suffice to say, I sniffle a lot and sneeze for a long time if I cuddle my pets a little too close.  When my allergies act up and my nose factory is running at full speed, a nice, soft tissue with lotion is what I need.  Even worse is when I have a cold and have the sore nose.<br /><br />These are two ply, like other reviewers stated.  They don\'t appear any thinner than a certain store brand that I buy at a -mart type of store.  The biggest differences between that store brand and these are the softness of the tissue (and not just because of the lotion, I don\'t think) and that I can blow my nose or sneeze hard and not wear shredded tissue on my shirt.  These hold up for regular use.  I appreciate that they can be purchased and delivered to your home in an econo pack, though I recommend that you be kind to your child\'s teacher and have some sent there for classroom use.  The kids and teacher will appreciate the softness.<br /><br />I do think they could upgrade the number of tissues in the box, because, yes, you will go through them quickly for a bad cold.',B07HSF5HTX,AGO75QZQCICU6SXOODFWLK677MHA
5,'I use this when I make Dr. Axe\'s vitamin C serum. Because of my skin allergies, there are very few oils that don\'t me to break out in hives.  I have friends that are also using Dr. Axe\'s recipe.  One friend in particular calls this stuff \"magic\".  I don\'t feel good about using animal products,  but we all have to draw a line somewhere. I\'ve used this product for years, periodically switching to something else, but always seem to go back to this brand.',B00J7R28QG,AG4L3NIJXN3YMQGB2DBCI75FMQIQ
