5,'This was recommended by The Strategist Editors on Slate, which is where I saw it.  It\'s exactly as they described it and the description on the website is dead on.  It\'d been a life saver for me.  I used to blind as a bat and wore glasses all of the time.  However I had cataract surgery about six months ago and  the surgeon corrected my distance visionsso I no longer need glasses.  The new lenses they inserted are multi-focal and for most things, they work great.  But they\'re not quite good enough for long reading sessions, needlework, or other close detail work.  As a result, I now have readers.  They were forever in the wrong place or I couldn\'t find them at all.  I purchased multiples of this product and now have specific places throughout the house for my readers.  When I take them off, I put them in the closest holder.  As I have multiple pairs of readers (kitchen, computer desk, needlework station, etc.), there is always one close at hand and exactly where I\'m looking.  It has the added benefit of the readers not longer interesting my cats, since the glasses are folded up so the earpieces are not accessible to be chewed on.  A win-win all the way around!',B06VVP9XBR,AH3LUW2X353BN4GW4IZI4YYHZ73A
