5,'Finally I can fall to sleep. I read 100+ reviews about this machine (and there were hundreds more to read) to make sure this was the last Sound Machine I would ever need. It really works. I, too, didn\'t see the need for 2-speed machine and cost was an issue. When I first turned it on I thought, &#34;Oh dear, this noise will never put me to sleep!&#34;. That was my first and last thought until I awoke several hours later.<br />I have really bad Tinnitus, which gets worse as the day turns into night. By the time I\'m ready to go to sleep, the ringing in my ear sounds like a bunch of kids screaming & yelling. When I awoke, I noticed that the \'ringing\' had subsided to a very low level.<br />My husband balked at the \'noise\' for about 10 seconds..., then all I heard was his slow, rhythmic breathing.<br />I decided to purchase 2 machines so that we could use one for our dog as she shakes and trembles from all the illegal fireworks that go off in our town during the whole summer tourist season. Our dog has her own little room set up with a cozy bed, her &#34;Thunder Shirt&#34; and the Sound Machine. She can\'t hear the fireworks with this machine so she\'s no longer in extreme distress! I prefer using the sound machine over giving her tranquilizers every time.',B000LQI2S0,AHIQBCSX23VFJDZCR3V7N2DM6BUQ
