4,'I actually own a previous model of this which is nowhere near as nice.  I bought this one because the older model is stuck 3 states away, and I\'m dealing with a minor foot issue.<br /><br />Some things that stand out:<br /><br />- the heating element.  If this heats from cold water, I assume it would take forever.  DO NOT expect it to do some miracle heating of cold or even cool water.  Start with lukewarm water, warm enough that you can tolerate it but not &#34;hot&#34; if that makes sense.  Then enable the heating element.  I estimate it will take roughly 15-30 minutes to actually &#34;heat&#34; the water from this point, just to give you perspective.  Plus your skin and vessels will thank you for the gradual heating.<br /><br />- the vibration element.  There\'s no real &#34;massaging&#34; here.  It just vibrates.  Good for the soles of your feet, yes.  That\'s about all it\'ll really do for you.  What irritated me is that the center separator has something in there that rattles a bit.  Not a showstopper but it was annoying.  (Yes, I removed the attachment piece.)<br /><br />- The bubble element.  I wasn\'t impressed.  It\'s good to help the water heat up faster by introducing air into it, but you literally can\'t feel the bubbles at your feet with the vibration element enabled.  Not nearly as dispersed or &#34;awesome&#34; as what the picture shows.<br /><br />- Some of the nubs under foot feel higher than others.  This is especially true near the pinky toe.  A bit annoying, not a showstopper.<br /><br />- I do like the separate compartment for storing the attachments.<br /><br />- I also like the way the pour spout is designed.  On the older model you could only go so high before water was spilling out the front.  Here, it\'s small enough to pour out but not so large as to cause spilling.<br /><br />- I did not use the rollers, I took them out.<br /><br />- I use a tea tree soak and they dissolve nicely here.  My feet are already looking and feeling much better after only a few days of sessions.<br /><br />- There are four attachments, one a regular brush, which you can use to completely pedicure.  I recommend following up with a foot lotion for the best results, or at least some cocoa butter lotion or coconut oil.',B00NMFUVZE,AGRBRL2U46HIDKDOKCDG5QVVW3LA
