3,'This scale was at first hard to set up.  It took a couple tries to get it to sync with the fitbit and app.  However, once that was accomplished it worked fine for several months.  Then, we found the light on in the middle of the night and a message saying &#34;Sensing&#34; and sometimes just a swirling image and sometimes a &#34;get off&#34; message - again, this is all discovered at night when no one is using the scale.  Apparently, its a common problem with the scale.  We found that removing the batteries and re-setting them usually fixed the problem, but this defect does cause it to run down batteries.<br />I still like the scale, in that it tracks my weight on my fitbit app - and shows long term trends, which are more useful than just today\'s weight.',B0077L8YFI,AEYPD25U362BSILYRFO7A2PU2GZA
2,'I purchased this to replace my prev heated eyelash curler that used batteries<br />Pros: gets hot pretty quickly<br />Easy to hold<br />Digital display is easy to read<br />Easy to turn on<br />Cons: the wand is straight but oh yeah my eye isn’t so it was difficult to curl my lashes all at once having to go in ‘sections’<br />Didn’t really curl - I did it with and without mascara<br />Bc it’s difficult to curl I kept touching my eyelid and it’s pretty hot ( pro and a con)<br /><br />Also as a side note- you see all these 5 star reviews? Well surprise there is a card in the box that says the company will you give you a choice of ‘gift’ for a 5 star review - I have to call them out bc it seems like you can’t trust reviews anymore with all these ‘bribes’ from companies<br /><br />If they would make the wand curved I think it would work much better - my old one (different company) was curved and worked great but I hated using all those batteries<br /><br />I’ll be returning',B07YCD2LRK,AGMFAZJDCVQKKKYUDIOWBQFF23DA
