1,'Ever spent more than you wanted to just because you thought you could get everything you needed all at once instead of building it yourself. The sad part of this product is that it could be great. The first aid products are a good start, and the backpack has padding with nice zippers. (Could use larger band-aids and gauze.)The trouble is that all the buckles and straps are made from super-slick material. (Unuseable, I have 30+ years of outdoor experience.) Strap on this pack, and it will simply slip off of you as all the straps come loose on their own. As if it was made by people that had pictures of a backpack but never used one. To use this product, you would need to replace all the buckles and straps or carry it in your arms like a pile of dirty Laundry. Buy your first aid gear separately and get a backpack that works. This one is a sad waste of money.',B01N7ZDNOB,AG4RG5LX5MUOKEV4QXD5DCBA3NJQ
