1,'This does not move easily on any terrain...only moves easily on flat smooth surfaces....have to lift it to get over the threshold unlike a rollator that moves over threshold easily.  The seat has you sitting on the handle in the middle of the seat...uncomfortable and can cause skin breakdown.  The brake cables are flopping about and catch on handles and obstacles as you go about.  Very tall and bulky hard to fit in a car.  There is no room for passengers if put in back seat and cannot fit in trunk if you want to close the trunk.  Even if it fits in your trunk...how are you going to walk to the car door once it is put in the back?  Does not allow you to walk much straight up unless you take very tiny steps because the seat is right at the knee if you stand straight up.  You have to lean forward just like any rollator to propel forward.  It is wobbly and feels unsafe as if the sides are loose.  Sitting is uncomfortable on it.  The walker is wider than a normal walker and harder to maneuver.  The bag is too flimsy to hold my portable oxygen...and falls off the walker when you are going down even a slight incline.  It is too prone to tip over which is unsafe for elderly and disabled.  I sent it back.  not for me.',B08VW76HJ1,AECMKJ74MQ2EV6DGD6EPD3W672ZA
