5,'This reshii has an intense earthy flavor.  In fact the flavor may be a little intense for some people at first.<br /><br />They\'ve done a decent job with high-quality re-sealable packaging, but longevity is still going to be a factor here. Herbs expire more quickly in powder form.  They start breaking down more rapidly when they\'re ground up so pay attention to the expiration date.  If you want reshii that lasts longer you should leave it in mushroom form and grind it yourself as needed.  As it is it\'s super-convenient to have it pre-ground, so IMO it\'s worth the convenience, but you\'ll have to decide for yourself - it\'s probably going to come down to how much and how often you\'re using it.<br /><br />Serving size is defined in \"scoops\" but it doesn\'t come with a scoop so there\'s no obvious way to tell what the correct volume for a serving is.  I started with a tablespoon, and the flavor was quite intense and the effects on my mental clarity were very apparent.  I worked my down to a teaspoon which I think would be more palatable for the average person.  The effects of the smaller portion were not as intense, but they seemed to last longer.  I would personally recommend a teaspoon three times a day - but you should follow the advice of your own herbalist (and if you don\'t have one, get one! lol).<br /><br />Overall this seems like a good value for the price, it\'s a good quality product and while the powder doesn\'t last as long as the mushroom itself, they provide an expiration date and good quality re-sealable packaging.',B07VRRK186,AENNTIQCHOHGLRH3DFVZUJDPOMBA
